{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-30100" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "In degrees, what is the general solution to the equation $\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=2?$ Assume that $n$ is an integer." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041314/state.json" "file_sha256" "0e17cca0af702060dade59144ebe1c83ee3a51200dcaecbaa370f96b12283949"} {"question" "q-30100" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we rearrange the equation and isolate $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{csc}⁡x & =2 \\\\ \\operatorname{csc}⁡x & =\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}.$ Therefore, the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=\\text{arcsin}(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})={45}^{∘}\n$$\n\nOur first solution lies in the $1$st quadrant and has a reference angle of ${\\theta }_{R}={45}^{∘}.$ Since $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x>0,$ the second solution must lie in the second quadrant, and it also has ${\\theta }_{R}={45}^{∘}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041314/assets/978eaf470ef3b61ff7839471ed4ac46f320922b4d30f7f95566095124d0526d7.png)\n\nSince the second solution ${x}_{2}$  lies in the $2$nd quadrant, we can find it using the reference angle as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & ={180}^{∘}-{\\theta }_{R} \\\\  & ={180}^{∘}-{45}^{∘} \\\\  & ={135}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the given equation is\n\n$$\nx={45}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘},\\,x={135}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041314/state.json" "file_sha256" "0e17cca0af702060dade59144ebe1c83ee3a51200dcaecbaa370f96b12283949"} {"question" "q-30100" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041314/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7d30fb21e1633aeffcf6ce6e18b8d4f23506a6e48e4a2e59a9342093e486263c"} {"question" "q-30100" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041314/state.json" "file_sha256" "0e17cca0af702060dade59144ebe1c83ee3a51200dcaecbaa370f96b12283949"} {"question" "q-30100" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x={135}^{∘}+n\\cdot {180}^{∘}"] ["math" "x={135}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘},\\,\\,x={225}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘}"] ["math" "x={45}^{∘}+n\\cdot {180}^{∘}"] ["math" "x={45}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘},\\,\\,x={135}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘}"] ["math" "x={45}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘},\\,\\,x={315}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041314/state.json" "file_sha256" "0e17cca0af702060dade59144ebe1c83ee3a51200dcaecbaa370f96b12283949"} {"question" "q-30100" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x={45}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘},\\,\\,x={135}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041314/state.json" "file_sha256" "0e17cca0af702060dade59144ebe1c83ee3a51200dcaecbaa370f96b12283949"} {"question" "q-120782" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solution to the equation $\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=-\\sqrt{3}.$ Assume that $n$ is an integer." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041314/state.json" "file_sha256" "0e17cca0af702060dade59144ebe1c83ee3a51200dcaecbaa370f96b12283949"} {"question" "q-120782" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that $\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}.$ Therefore, the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x} & =-\\sqrt{3} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3})=-\\frac{\\pi }{6}\n$$\n\nThe tangent function has a period of $\\pi .$  Hence, the general solution for the given equation is\n\n$$\nx=-\\frac{\\pi }{6}+n\\pi .\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041314/state.json" "file_sha256" "0e17cca0af702060dade59144ebe1c83ee3a51200dcaecbaa370f96b12283949"} {"question" "q-120782" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041314/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7d30fb21e1633aeffcf6ce6e18b8d4f23506a6e48e4a2e59a9342093e486263c"} {"question" "q-120782" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041314/state.json" "file_sha256" "0e17cca0af702060dade59144ebe1c83ee3a51200dcaecbaa370f96b12283949"} {"question" "q-120782" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x=-\\frac{2\\pi }{3}+n\\pi "] ["math" "x=-\\frac{5\\pi }{6}+n\\pi "] ["math" "x=-\\frac{\\pi }{6}+n\\pi "] ["math" "x=\\frac{4\\pi }{3}+n\\pi "] ["math" "x=\\frac{7\\pi }{6}+n\\pi "]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041314/state.json" "file_sha256" "0e17cca0af702060dade59144ebe1c83ee3a51200dcaecbaa370f96b12283949"} {"question" "q-120782" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x=-\\frac{\\pi }{6}+n\\pi "] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041314/state.json" "file_sha256" "0e17cca0af702060dade59144ebe1c83ee3a51200dcaecbaa370f96b12283949"} {"question" "q-274743" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041314/assets/c21ae590fc35738a016fd9c6191bd15685d0d0a6fb043f32aafaf8d01845d149.png)\n\nThe graph above shows a portion of the curve $y=2\\operatorname{tan}⁡x$ and the line $y=2\\sqrt{3}.$\nFind an expression of the form\n$x=\\theta +n\\cdot b,$\nwhere $\\theta \\in [0,\\pi ),$ $n$ is an integer and $b$ is the period in radians, that generates the $x$-coordinates of the points of intersection.\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}\n$+\\,n\\,\\cdot $\n{{field-2}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041314/state.json" "file_sha256" "0e17cca0af702060dade59144ebe1c83ee3a51200dcaecbaa370f96b12283949"} {"question" "q-274743" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "At the intersection points, the $y$-values are the same for both graphs. This gives the equation\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=2\\sqrt{3} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\sqrt{3})=\\frac{\\pi }{3}.\n$$\n\nThe tangent function has a period of $\\pi .$  Hence, the general solution for the given equation is \n\n$$\nx=\\frac{\\pi }{3}+n\\cdot \\pi .\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041314/state.json" "file_sha256" "0e17cca0af702060dade59144ebe1c83ee3a51200dcaecbaa370f96b12283949"} {"question" "q-274743" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041314/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7d30fb21e1633aeffcf6ce6e18b8d4f23506a6e48e4a2e59a9342093e486263c"} {"question" "q-274743" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041314/state.json" "file_sha256" "0e17cca0af702060dade59144ebe1c83ee3a51200dcaecbaa370f96b12283949"} {"question" "q-274743" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\pi}{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041314/state.json" "file_sha256" "0e17cca0af702060dade59144ebe1c83ee3a51200dcaecbaa370f96b12283949"} {"question" "q-274743" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041314/state.json" "file_sha256" "0e17cca0af702060dade59144ebe1c83ee3a51200dcaecbaa370f96b12283949"} {"question" "q-274743" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\pi"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041314/state.json" "file_sha256" "0e17cca0af702060dade59144ebe1c83ee3a51200dcaecbaa370f96b12283949"} {"question" "q-323844" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solution to the equation $\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}-1}$ in the form $x=\\theta +n\\cdot b$ where $\\theta \\in [0,{180}^{∘}),$ $n$ is an integer and $b$ is the period in degrees.\n\n*Hint: You may use the fact that $tan\\,({157.5}^{∘})=1-\\sqrt{2}.$*\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}${}^{∘}+\\,n\\,\\cdot $\n{{field-2}}${}^{∘}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041314/state.json" "file_sha256" "0e17cca0af702060dade59144ebe1c83ee3a51200dcaecbaa370f96b12283949"} {"question" "q-323844" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that $\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}.$ Therefore, the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x} & =-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}-1} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =1-\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(1-\\sqrt{2})={157.5}^{∘}\n$$\n\nThe tangent function has a period of ${180}^{∘}.$  Hence, the general solution for the given equation is\n\n$$\nx={157.5}^{∘}+n\\cdot {180}^{∘}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041314/state.json" "file_sha256" "0e17cca0af702060dade59144ebe1c83ee3a51200dcaecbaa370f96b12283949"} {"question" "q-323844" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041314/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7d30fb21e1633aeffcf6ce6e18b8d4f23506a6e48e4a2e59a9342093e486263c"} {"question" "q-323844" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041314/state.json" "file_sha256" "0e17cca0af702060dade59144ebe1c83ee3a51200dcaecbaa370f96b12283949"} {"question" "q-323844" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "157.5"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041314/state.json" "file_sha256" "0e17cca0af702060dade59144ebe1c83ee3a51200dcaecbaa370f96b12283949"} {"question" "q-323844" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041314/state.json" "file_sha256" "0e17cca0af702060dade59144ebe1c83ee3a51200dcaecbaa370f96b12283949"} {"question" "q-323844" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "180"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041314/state.json" "file_sha256" "0e17cca0af702060dade59144ebe1c83ee3a51200dcaecbaa370f96b12283949"} {"question" "q-324057" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041314/assets/435dd125850e3f97b5c3753a027f2db8718131ab499ef6711eaac637b1a022bd.png)\n\nThe graph shows a portion of the curve $y=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ and the line $y=1.$ Find expressions of the form\n\n$$\nx={\\theta }_{1}+n\\cdot b,\\,x={\\theta }_{2}+n\\cdot b,\n$$\n\nwhere ${\\theta }_{1}<{\\theta }_{2},$ ${\\theta }_{1},{\\theta }_{2}\\in [0,2\\pi ),$ $b$ is the period in radians, and $n$ is an integer, that generate the $x$-values of all of their points of intersection.\n\n${\\theta }_{1}=${{field-1}}$,\\,{\\theta }_{2}=$\n{{field-2}}$,\\,b=$\n{{field-3}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041314/state.json" "file_sha256" "0e17cca0af702060dade59144ebe1c83ee3a51200dcaecbaa370f96b12283949"} {"question" "q-324057" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "At the intersection points, the $y$-values are the same for both graphs. This gives the equation\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & =1 \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡x & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=arcsin\\,(\\frac{1}{2})=\\frac{\\pi }{6}.\n$$\n\nOur first solution lies in the $1$st quadrant and has a reference angle of ${\\theta }_{R}=\\frac{\\pi }{6}.$ Since $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x>0,$ the second solution must lie in the $2$nd quadrant and it also has ${\\theta }_{R}=\\frac{\\pi }{6}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041314/assets/b0738a8a505b89ff687cb4de350a00f2e10d6209fbeee7dcdfdf0ee359a9cc3c.png)\n\nSince the second solution ${x}_{2}$ lies in the $2$nd quadrant, we can find it using the reference angle as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & =\\pi -{\\theta }_{R} \\\\  & =\\pi -\\frac{\\pi }{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\pi }{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solutions are\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{\\pi }{6}+2\\pi n,\\,x=\\frac{5\\pi }{6}+2\\pi n.\n$$\n\nTherefore, since ${\\theta }_{1}<{\\theta }_{2},$ we have ${\\theta }_{1}=\\frac{\\pi }{6},\\text{ }{\\theta }_{2}=\\frac{5\\pi }{6},\\text{ }\\text{and}\\text{ }b=2\\pi .$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041314/state.json" "file_sha256" "0e17cca0af702060dade59144ebe1c83ee3a51200dcaecbaa370f96b12283949"} {"question" "q-324057" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041314/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7d30fb21e1633aeffcf6ce6e18b8d4f23506a6e48e4a2e59a9342093e486263c"} {"question" "q-324057" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041314/state.json" "file_sha256" "0e17cca0af702060dade59144ebe1c83ee3a51200dcaecbaa370f96b12283949"} {"question" "q-324057" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\pi}{6}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041314/state.json" "file_sha256" "0e17cca0af702060dade59144ebe1c83ee3a51200dcaecbaa370f96b12283949"} {"question" "q-324057" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041314/state.json" "file_sha256" "0e17cca0af702060dade59144ebe1c83ee3a51200dcaecbaa370f96b12283949"} {"question" "q-324057" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{5\\pi}{6}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041314/state.json" "file_sha256" "0e17cca0af702060dade59144ebe1c83ee3a51200dcaecbaa370f96b12283949"} {"question" "q-324057" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041314/state.json" "file_sha256" "0e17cca0af702060dade59144ebe1c83ee3a51200dcaecbaa370f96b12283949"} {"question" "q-324057" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2\\pi"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041314/state.json" "file_sha256" "0e17cca0af702060dade59144ebe1c83ee3a51200dcaecbaa370f96b12283949"}] "usage" {"q-30100" []} "basis" 1494 "retractions" [[17592186101278 :question/problem "In degrees, what is the general solution to the equation $\\sqrt{2}\\csc x = 2$? Assume that $n$ is an integer."]] "immutable_answers" [17592186099299 17592186099300 17592186099301 17592186099302 17592186099303] "immutable_fields" [[17592186099298 :answer-field/correct] [17592186099298 :answer-field/id] [17592186099298 :answer-field/key] [17592186099298 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
